# QuantOS environment template.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in locally. `.env` is gitignored; this template must never hold a
# real value.
#
# Credentials are read from the process environment by
# `quant_system.data.upstox.UpstoxClient`. `quant_system.config.env.load_env_file` loads the
# nearest `.env` into `os.environ` at the launcher entry point, so a filled `.env` is visible
# without a dotenv library. Exporting in the shell works too:
#
#   PowerShell:  $env:UPSTOX_ANALYTICS_TOKEN = "<token>"
#   bash:        export UPSTOX_ANALYTICS_TOKEN="<token>"
#
# Format rules enforced by the parser: `KEY=value`, no spaces around `=`, no trailing comment on
# the line, value on a single line. One matching pair of quotes is stripped. A leading `export `
# is tolerated. A duplicated key silently takes the LAST occurrence in the file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UPSTOX TOKENS — which one you use decides whether this system needs a daily manual refresh.
# Both were measured against the live API on 2026-08-31. These are HTTP results, not docs.
#
# 1. ANALYTICS TOKEN — one per user, no cost, ~1 year validity. Generated from the Upstox
#    developer console, which also offers a Revoke control. MEASURED: it authenticates the live
#    quote feed. This is the token an unattended paper pilot wants, because it does not expire
#    nightly.
#
# 2. ACCESS TOKEN — standard OAuth token, expires 03:30 IST the morning after issue. Upstox V2
#    issues no refresh token, so renewal means repeating the login flow every trading day before
#    ~09:15 IST.
#
# Measured, analytics token unless noted:
#   v2 /market-quote/quotes  (1 instrument)   -> HTTP 200
#   v2 /market-quote/quotes  (10 batched)     -> HTTP 200, all 10 with depth + volume
#   v2 /market-quote/ltp                      -> HTTP 200
#   v3 /historical-candle/intraday/.../1min   -> HTTP 200
#   v3 + v2 /historical-candle/...            -> HTTP 200 with NO Authorization header at all
#   v2 /user/profile                          -> HTTP 401 UDAPI1221 (static-IP note below)
#
# So: historical bar acquisition needs no token whatsoever, and live quotes — therefore live
# paper trading, which must mark positions against a real price — are satisfied by the analytics
# token for a year at a time. Placing no orders exempts you from the order API, not from the
# quote API; but the quote API does not require the *daily* token.
#
# Two caveats that must travel with the above:
#   - The analytics token carries an `isExtended` claim, so it is an extended-token variant. An
#     earlier revision of this file claimed extended tokens cannot read market quotes. That was
#     wrong, and the 200s above disprove it.
#   - /user/profile returns UDAPI1221: "permitted only when requested from the static IP
#     configured in your account". Some endpoints are IP-bound for this token class. Quotes,
#     batched quotes and intraday candles were NOT affected from the development machine, but a
#     deployment from a different IP should re-run the probe rather than assume.
#
# With no token configured at all, governed acquisition returns a non-retryable
# PROVIDER_UNAUTHORIZED outcome and the bundled server and daily pipeline run on SYNTHETIC bars.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Upstox analytics token. Long-lived (~1 year), one per user, free, authenticates market quotes.
# Preferred for unattended sessions. JWT: three dot-separated segments, ~335 characters.
UPSTOX_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=

# Upstox standard access token. Expires 03:30 IST the morning after it is issued.
UPSTOX_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Upstox API key. Retained for source compatibility; V3 historical data authenticates with a
# bearer token, not this value.
UPSTOX_API_KEY=

# Upstox API secret. Used for programmatic OAuth token renewal.
UPSTOX_API_SECRET=
